import Mathlib
import BookProof.ChapterBookBrstGaugeFixing
import BookProof.ChapterBrstHarmonicDecomposition

/-!
# "Longitudinal = exact": the pure-gauge directions are the ones the BRST charge produces

Plan: `softmodes.md`, Phase 1, open item 3 — *"'Longitudinal = exact'.  The claim `H_phys`
contains no longitudinal soft zero-mode is the identification `closure (range Ω) = span{∂ᵢφ}`
(the pure-gauge directions are precisely the BRST-exact states), followed by the observation
that a longitudinal plane wave is not harmonic, i.e. is not in `ker Ω ∩ ker Ω*`."*

That item has two halves of very different character, and this development closes both — in
separate places, because they are genuinely separate theorems.

## 1. The identification, in the realization of `book.tex`

`ChapterBookBrstYangMills` *realizes* the charge of `book.tex` on the graded state space
`BookState N = MvPolynomial (Fin 4 × Fin N) ℂ ⊗ ExteriorAlgebra ℂ (Fin N → ℂ)`, the coordinates
`X (μ, a)` being the gauge-field components `A_{μa}`.  In that realization the infinitesimal
gauge orbit of the coordinate `X (μ, a)` generated by `T_c` is the symbol

`gaussVec G c (μ, a) = −(D_μ)_{ca} + Σ_g f_{agc} X (μ, g)`

(`gaussVec`, `ChapterBookBrstYangMills`), an *affine* polynomial: a constant plus a linear part.

* **the constant term `−(D_μ)_{ca}` is the longitudinal direction** — it is `∂_μ α_a` for the
  gauge parameter `α = T_c`, and it is field-independent, which is exactly what a gradient is;
  `longitudinalGaugeVec` isolates it;
* the linear term `Σ_g f_{agc} X (μ, g)` is the **non-abelian commutator** `[A_μ, α]_a`, which
  is *not* a gradient; `commGaugeVec` isolates it, and `gaussVec_eq_longitudinal_add_comm`
  is the split;
* in the **abelian** case the commutator part is absent and the orbit is purely longitudinal
  (`gaussVec_eq_longitudinal_of_abelian`).  That is the setting in which "the pure-gauge
  directions are the gradients" is literally true, and it is the setting of the theorem below.

**`comm_bookOmega_Afield`** is the content of the item: in the abelian case the book's charge
reduces to its derivative term (`bookOmega_abelian`), so its commutator with `A_{μa}` is fixed
by the canonical relation `bookCCR` and comes out to be

`[Ω, A_{μa}] = −i · dChi G μ a`,

where `dChi G μ a = Σ_b (D_μ)_{ba} ψ†_b` is **the ghost-dressed longitudinal direction** — nothing
else.  So the BRST variation of the field *is* the longitudinal direction: the directions the
reduction removes are exactly the ones the charge produces.

`longitudinal_mem_exactStates_of_physical` is the immediate payoff: applied to a BRST-closed
state `v`, `bookOmega G (Afield μ a v) = −i · dChi G μ a v`, so **the ghost-dressed longitudinal
direction applied to a physical state is BRST-exact** — the longitudinal sector maps to zero in
the cohomology, which is the plan's "no longitudinal soft zero-mode", at the level of the
algebraic realization.

## 1b. The non-abelian case: `[Ω, A_{μa}]` in full

For `f ≠ 0` the quartic term of `bookOmega` does not drop out, and §4 computes the commutator
in full: **`comm_bookOmega_Afield_nonabelian`**, `[Ω, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −i · dChi G μ₀ a₀
+ i · Σ_{b,c} f_{a₀bc} A_{μ₀b} ψ†_c`.  The first summand is the longitudinal direction of §2;
the second is `−i·` the commutator part `commGaugeVec` of the gauge orbit.  For `f = 0` the
second sum vanishes (`commGaugeVec_eq_zero_of_abelian`) and the statement reduces to
`comm_bookOmega_Afield` — so §2 is the abelian special case of §4, not an independent theorem.
The tooling is §4's own: `Afield_comm_Afield`, `ghostOpN_comm_Afield` (hence
`ghostCubic_comm_Afield`), `quartic_comm_Afield`, and `comm_deriv_Afield`, the derivative-term
commutator extracted from §2 so both cases share one proof.

## 2. The conclusion, in the abstract Hilbert space

`ChapterBrstHarmonicDecomposition` proves the orthogonal decomposition
`H = closure(range Ω) ⊕ (ker Ω ∩ ker Ω†)`.  Given that, "a longitudinal state is not harmonic"
is a *consequence*, not a further hypothesis — and it is stated there, for an arbitrary
subspace `L ≤ exactStates`, as `no_longitudinal_zero_mode`.  It needs no field model: it holds
for whatever "longitudinal" means, provided the identification of §1 puts it inside the exact
states.

## Honest boundary

* The **equality** `closure (range Ω) = span{∂ᵢφ}` is proved here in one direction and in the
  abelian case: the longitudinal (gradient) direction is BRST-produced
  (`comm_bookOmega_Afield`, `longitudinal_mem_exactStates_of_physical`).  The converse inclusion
  needs a model in which the gauge field is a *function on spacetime*, so that `span{∂ᵢφ}` is a
  subspace of a Hilbert space to be compared with `closure (range Ω)`.  The realization of
  `book.tex` carried here is the single-multiplet one: spacetime dependence enters only through
  the matrix `G.D`, and `BookState N` carries no inner product and no completion.  So the
  identification is an identity of *operators*, not yet an equality of *closures of subspaces*.
* The **non-abelian** case has the extra commutator term `Σ_{bc} f_{abc} A_{μb} ψ†_c` (times
  `−i`) in `[bookOmega G, Afield μ a]`; **this is now a theorem** —
  `comm_bookOmega_Afield_nonabelian`, §4, which reads
  `[Ω, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −i · dChi G μ₀ a₀ + i · Σ_{b,c} f_{a₀bc} A_{μ₀b} ψ†_c`, i.e.
  `−i (D_{μ₀}ψ†)_{a₀}`.  The mechanism is that the extra field and ghost factors of the quartic
  term (`A_{μb}` a multiplication operator, `ψ†_c` on the other tensor factor) commute with
  `A_{μ₀a₀}`, so the whole commutator collapses onto `[π^μ_a, A_{μ₀a₀}]`; the cubic ghost term
  drops out because it is a pure ghost operator (`ghostCubic_comm_Afield`).  That second summand
  is `−i·` the commutator part `commGaugeVec` of the orbit, not a gradient, so in the non-abelian
  theory "the gauge orbit" is still strictly larger than "the longitudinal span", and the
  identification must be read as `longitudinal ⊆ gauge orbit = exact`.  What remains unclaimed
  for `f ≠ 0` is the *converse* inclusion `exact ⊆ span{∂ᵢφ}`, and the equality of closures —
  both blocked by the missing spacetime dependence of `BookState N`, as in the bullet above.
* Both parts are about the *charge*, not about a completed `H_phys`: §1 is algebraic on
  `BookState`, §2 is abstract on a Hilbert space with a bounded charge.  The unbounded
  (`ChapterBrstUnbounded`) twin of §2 is the same argument.

Everything below is `sorry`-free and `axiom`-free.
-/

namespace BookProof.BrstLongitudinal

open BookProof.BookBrstYangMills BookProof.BookBrstGaugeFixing
open BookProof.BRSTNilpotent BookProof.QuantumGravityBrstCharge
open MvPolynomial

noncomputable section

variable {N : ℕ} (G : GaugeAlgebra N)

/-! ## 1. The longitudinal part of the gauge orbit -/

/-- **The longitudinal (pure-gauge) part of the gauge orbit of `A_{μa}`**: the field-independent
term `−∂_μ α_a` of the infinitesimal gauge transformation of the coordinate `X (μ, a)` generated
by `T_c`, with `∂_μ` the matrix `G.D` of the book's single-multiplet realization.  It is constant
as a polynomial — it does not see the gauge field — which is precisely what makes it a gradient
direction rather than a field-dependent one. -/
def longitudinalGaugeVec (c : Fin N) (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) : FieldPoly N :=
  ((-(G.D μ c a) : ℝ) : ℂ) • (1 : FieldPoly N)

/-- The non-abelian (commutator) part of the gauge orbit of `A_{μa}`: `[A_μ, α]_a`, linear in the
gauge field and present only for `f ≠ 0`. -/
def commGaugeVec (c : Fin N) (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) : FieldPoly N :=
  ∑ g, ((G.f a g c : ℝ) : ℂ) • X (μ, g)

/-- **The gauge orbit splits into a longitudinal part and a commutator part.** -/
theorem gaussVec_eq_longitudinal_add_comm (c : Fin N) (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) :
    gaussVec G c (μ, a) = longitudinalGaugeVec G c μ a + commGaugeVec G c μ a := by
  simp only [gaussVec, vecComb, longitudinalGaugeVec, commGaugeVec]

/-- **For an abelian gauge algebra the gauge orbit is purely longitudinal**: the commutator part
is the only field-dependent piece and it vanishes, so the infinitesimal transformation of
`A_{μa}` is exactly `∂_μ α_a`. -/
theorem gaussVec_eq_longitudinal_of_abelian (hab : ∀ a b c : Fin N, G.f a b c = 0)
    (c : Fin N) (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) :
    gaussVec G c (μ, a) = longitudinalGaugeVec G c μ a := by
  have h0 : commGaugeVec G c μ a = 0 := by
    rw [commGaugeVec]
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun g _ => ?_
    rw [hab, Complex.ofReal_zero, zero_smul]
  rw [gaussVec_eq_longitudinal_add_comm, h0, add_zero]

/-- **`dChi G μ a` is the ghost-dressed longitudinal direction**: `∂_μ α_a` with the ghost `ψ†`
attached.  This is the object the BRST charge produces when it varies `A_{μa}`. -/
theorem dChi_eq_longitudinal_dress (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) :
    dChi G μ a = ∑ b, ((G.D μ b a : ℝ) : ℂ) • chiOp b := rfl

/-! ## 2. The BRST variation of the field is the longitudinal direction -/

/-- A sum of `ℝ`-scalar multiples of operators vanishes when the scalars do. -/
theorem sum_smul_end_eq_zero {T : Fin N → Fin N → Fin N → Module.End ℂ (BookState N)}
    (hab : ∀ a b c : Fin N, G.f a b c = 0) :
    ((∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N, (G.f a b c) • T a b c)
      : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) = 0 := by
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun a _ => Finset.sum_eq_zero fun b _ =>
    Finset.sum_eq_zero fun c _ => ?_
  rw [hab, zero_smul]

/-- In the abelian case the book's BRST charge reduces to its derivative term: the two
`f`-carrying summands of `bookOmega` vanish. -/
theorem bookOmega_abelian (hab : ∀ a b c : Fin N, G.f a b c = 0) :
    bookOmega G = (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a) := by
  have hquartic : (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
      (G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c)) = 0 := by
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun μ _ => sum_smul_end_eq_zero G hab
  have hcubic : (∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
      (G.f a b c) • (chiOp a * chiOp b * betaOp c)) = 0 :=
    sum_smul_end_eq_zero G hab
  rw [bookOmega, hquartic, hcubic, smul_zero]
  abel

/-- The ghosts commute with the gauge field, hence so does `dChi`. -/
theorem smul_end_comm {r : ℂ} {S T : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)} (h : S * T = T * S) :
    (r • S) * T = T * (r • S) := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  rw [Module.End.mul_apply, Module.End.mul_apply,
    LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, map_smul]
  have h' : S (T x) = T (S x) := by
    rw [← Module.End.mul_apply, ← Module.End.mul_apply, h]
  rw [h']

/-- A scalar times the identity is central. -/
theorem smul_one_mul_end (r : ℂ) (T : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) :
    (r • (1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N))) * T = r • T := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  rw [Module.End.mul_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, Module.End.one_apply,
    LinearMap.smul_apply]

theorem dChi_comm_Afield (μ0 : Fin 4) (a0 : Fin N) (ν : Fin 4) (b : Fin N) :
    dChi G ν b * Afield μ0 a0 = Afield μ0 a0 * dChi G ν b := by
  rw [dChi, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun c _ => ?_
  exact smul_end_comm (Afield_comm_chi μ0 a0 c).symm

/-- **The derivative term of the charge commutes with the field.**  This is the piece of
`bookOmega` that survives in the abelian limit; its commutator with `A_{μ₀a₀}` is computed from
`bookCCR` alone and is `−i · dChi G μ₀ a₀`.  Stated separately from `comm_bookOmega_Afield` so
that the non-abelian theorem can reuse it. -/
theorem comm_deriv_Afield (μ0 : Fin 4) (a0 : Fin N) :
    (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a) * Afield μ0 a0
        - Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a)
      = -((Complex.I : ℂ) • dChi G μ0 a0) := by
  have hterm : ∀ (ν : Fin 4) (b : Fin N),
      mom ν b * dChi G ν b * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b * dChi G ν b
        = -((if (μ0, a0) = (ν, b)
            then ((Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) * dChi G ν b) else 0)) := by
    intro ν b
    have hcc : mom ν b * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b
        = -((if (μ0, a0) = (ν, b)
            then (Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) else 0)) := by
      have hrearr : mom ν b * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b
          = -((Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b) - (mom ν b * Afield μ0 a0)) := by abel
      rw [hrearr, bookCCR μ0 ν a0 b]
    have hstep : mom ν b * dChi G ν b * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b * dChi G ν b
        = (mom ν b * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b) * dChi G ν b := by
      rw [mul_assoc, dChi_comm_Afield G μ0 a0 ν b, ← mul_assoc]
      exact (sub_mul (mom ν b * Afield μ0 a0) (Afield μ0 a0 * mom ν b)
        (dChi G ν b)).symm
    rw [hstep, hcc]
    refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
    simp only [Module.End.mul_apply]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  have hsplit : (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a) * Afield μ0 a0
      - Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a)
      = ∑ μ : Fin 4, ((∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a) * Afield μ0 a0
        - Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a)) := by
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
    exact (Finset.sum_sub_distrib
      (f := fun i => (∑ a : Fin N, mom i a * dChi G i a) * Afield μ0 a0)
      (g := fun i => Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ a : Fin N, mom i a * dChi G i a))).symm
  rw [hsplit]
  have hinner : ∀ μ : Fin 4,
      ((∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a) * Afield μ0 a0
        - Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ a : Fin N, mom μ a * dChi G μ a))
      = ∑ b : Fin N, (mom μ b * dChi G μ b * Afield μ0 a0
        - Afield μ0 a0 * mom μ b * dChi G μ b) := by
    intro μ
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun a _ =>
      (mul_assoc (Afield μ0 a0) (mom μ a) (dChi G μ a)).symm]
    exact (Finset.sum_sub_distrib
      (f := fun a => mom μ a * dChi G μ a * Afield μ0 a0)
      (g := fun a => Afield μ0 a0 * mom μ a * dChi G μ a)).symm
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => hinner μ]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => hterm μ b]
  have houter : ∀ μ : Fin 4, μ ≠ μ0 →
      ∑ b : Fin N,
        (-(if (μ0, a0) = (μ, b) then (Complex.I • 1) * dChi G μ b else 0)) = 0 := by
    intro μ hμ
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun b _ => ?_
    by_cases h : (μ0, a0) = (μ, b)
    · have hm : μ0 = μ := congrArg Prod.fst h
      exact absurd hm hμ.symm
    · rw [if_neg h]
      norm_num
  have hinner0 : ∀ b : Fin N, b ≠ a0 →
      (-(if (μ0, a0) = (μ0, b) then (Complex.I • 1) * dChi G μ0 b else 0)) = 0 := by
    intro b hb
    by_cases h : (μ0, a0) = (μ0, b)
    · have ha : a0 = b := congrArg Prod.snd h
      exact absurd ha (Ne.symm hb)
    · rw [if_neg h]
      norm_num
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single μ0 (fun μ _ hμ => houter μ hμ)
    (fun hh => absurd (Finset.mem_univ _) hh)]
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single a0 (fun b _ hb => hinner0 b hb)
    (fun hh => absurd (Finset.mem_univ _) hh)]
  rw [if_pos rfl, smul_one_mul]

/-- **The BRST variation of the gauge field is the longitudinal direction.**  For an abelian
gauge algebra the book's charge is the derivative term alone, so the canonical relation `bookCCR`
computes its commutator with `A_{μa}` exactly:

`[Ω, A_{μa}] = −i · ∂_μ α_a` dressed with the ghost.

No commutator piece appears, because there is none.  This is the algebraic content of
"longitudinal = exact": **the directions the BRST reduction removes are precisely the ones the
charge produces.** -/
theorem comm_bookOmega_Afield (hab : ∀ a b c : Fin N, G.f a b c = 0) (μ0 : Fin 4) (a0 : Fin N) :
    bookOmega G * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * bookOmega G
      = -((Complex.I : ℂ) • dChi G μ0 a0) := by
  rw [bookOmega_abelian G hab, comm_deriv_Afield G μ0 a0]

/-- **The longitudinal sector is BRST-exact where it matters.**  Applied to a BRST-closed state
`v` (`Ω v = 0`), the identity `comm_bookOmega_Afield` reads

`bookOmega G (Afield μ a v) = −i · dChi G μ a v`,

so the ghost-dressed longitudinal direction is in the image of the charge: it is BRST-exact, and
its class in `brstCohomology` is zero.  This is `softmodes.md` Phase 1's "no longitudinal soft
zero-mode" at the level the algebraic realization supports. -/
theorem longitudinal_mem_exactStates_of_physical (hab : ∀ a b c : Fin N, G.f a b c = 0)
    (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) {v : BookState N} (hv : v ∈ physicalStates G) :
    ⇑(-((Complex.I : ℂ) • dChi G μ a)) v ∈ exactStates G := by
  refine ⟨Afield μ a v, ?_⟩
  have h : bookOmega G (Afield μ a v) - Afield μ a (bookOmega G v)
      = (-(Complex.I • dChi G μ a)) v :=
    congrArg (fun T : Module.End ℂ (BookState N) => T v) (comm_bookOmega_Afield G hab μ a)
  rw [physicalStates, LinearMap.mem_ker] at hv
  rw [hv, map_zero, sub_zero] at h
  exact h

/-! ## 3. The non-abelian case -/

/-- **The longitudinal part is exactly the spacetime-derivative term**, and it does not see the
structure constants at all: it vanishes precisely where `G.D` vanishes at that index.  So the
longitudinal direction is present — and is the same direction — whether or not the gauge algebra
is abelian.  What the non-abelian case adds is the *commutator* part on top of it. -/
theorem longitudinalGaugeVec_eq_zero_iff (c : Fin N) (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) :
    longitudinalGaugeVec G c μ a = 0 ↔ G.D μ c a = 0 := by
  rw [longitudinalGaugeVec, smul_eq_zero, Complex.ofReal_eq_zero, neg_eq_zero]
  simp

/-- **The commutator part vanishes identically for an abelian gauge algebra.**  It is the only
field-dependent piece of the gauge orbit, so for `f = 0` the orbit is *exactly* the longitudinal
span — the identification `gauge orbit = longitudinal` is an equality, not merely an inclusion.
For `f ≠ 0` it is strictly larger, and the honest reading of "longitudinal = exact" is
`longitudinal ⊆ gauge orbit = exact`. -/
theorem commGaugeVec_eq_zero_of_abelian (hab : ∀ a b c : Fin N, G.f a b c = 0)
    (c : Fin N) (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) : commGaugeVec G c μ a = 0 := by
  rw [commGaugeVec]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun g _ => ?_
  rw [hab, Complex.ofReal_zero, zero_smul]

/-! ## 4. The non-abelian commutator `[Ω, A_{μa}]`

The note above recorded the field-dependent piece of `[Ω, A_{μa}]` as *"a shape, not a
theorem"*.  It is a theorem now.

Of the three terms of `bookOmega`, only the quartic one `−Σ f_{abc} π^μ_a A_{μb} ψ†_c` can
contribute beyond the derivative term, and inside it only `π^μ_a` fails to commute with
`A_{μ₀a₀}`: `A_{μb}` is a multiplication operator and `ψ†_c` lives on the ghost tensor factor.
So the whole commutator collapses onto `[π^μ_a, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −δ · i`, and what is left is
exactly

`[Ω, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −i ∂_{μ₀}ψ†_{a₀} + i Σ_{b,c} f_{a₀bc} A_{μ₀b} ψ†_c`,

i.e. `[Ω, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −i (D_{μ₀} ψ†)_{a₀}`.  The **first** term is the ghost-dressed
longitudinal direction of `comm_bookOmega_Afield`; the **second** is the commutator part
`[A_μ, α]`, which is `−i` times `commGaugeVec`.  The cubic ghost term drops out because it is a
pure ghost operator.  For `f = 0` the second summand vanishes identically and the statement
reduces to `comm_bookOmega_Afield`.

This is the precise sense in which the non-abelian gauge orbit is *strictly larger* than the
longitudinal span: the charge varies `A_{μa}` in the full covariant direction, and the extra
term is field-dependent, hence not a gradient. -/

/-- Two gauge-field (multiplication) operators commute. -/
theorem Afield_comm_Afield (μ ν : Fin 4) (a b : Fin N) :
    Afield (N := N) μ a * Afield ν b = Afield ν b * Afield μ a := by
  rw [Afield, Afield, ← bosOpN_mul, ← bosOpN_mul]
  refine congrArg bosOpN ?_
  refine LinearMap.ext fun p => ?_
  rw [Module.End.mul_apply, Module.End.mul_apply, AfieldPoly_apply, AfieldPoly_apply]
  exact mul_left_comm _ _ _

/-- A ghost operator commutes with the gauge field: they act on different tensor factors. -/
theorem ghostOpN_comm_Afield (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) (T : Module.End ℂ (GhostSpace N)) :
    ghostOpN T * Afield μ a = Afield μ a * ghostOpN T :=
  (bosOpN_ghostOpN_comm (AfieldPoly μ a) T).symm

/-- The ghost annihilation operators commute with the gauge field. -/
theorem betaOp_comm_Afield (μ : Fin 4) (a b : Fin N) :
    betaOp (N := N) b * Afield μ a = Afield μ a * betaOp b :=
  ghostOpN_comm_Afield μ a _

/-- **The cubic ghost term of the charge commutes with the gauge field.**  It is built entirely
from `ψ†`, `ψ`, so it never meets `A_{μa}`. -/
theorem ghostCubic_comm_Afield (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N) :
    (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N, ∑ e : Fin N,
        (G.f b c e) • (chiOp b * chiOp c * betaOp e)) * Afield μ a
      = Afield μ a * (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N, ∑ e : Fin N,
        (G.f b c e) • (chiOp b * chiOp c * betaOp e)) := by
  classical
  have hS : ∀ b c e : Fin N,
      (chiOp (N := N) b * chiOp c * betaOp e) * Afield μ a
        = Afield μ a * (chiOp b * chiOp c * betaOp e) := by
    intro b c e
    have h1 : chiOp (N := N) b * chiOp c * betaOp e
        = ghostOpN (ghostCreN b * ghostCreN c * ghostAnnN e) := by
      rw [chiOp, chiOp, betaOp, ← ghostOpN_mul, ← ghostOpN_mul]
    rw [h1]
    exact ghostOpN_comm_Afield μ a _
  simp only [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun c _ =>
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun e _ => by rw [smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, hS b c e]

/-- `[U·V, W] = [U, W]·V` as soon as `V` commutes with `W`: the extra factor passes straight
through the commutator. -/
theorem commutator_mul_right {U V W : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)} (h : V * W = W * V) :
    U * V * W - W * (U * V) = (U * W - W * U) * V := by
  rw [mul_assoc U V W, h, ← mul_assoc U W V, ← mul_assoc W U V, ← sub_mul]

/-- **The quartic term of the charge against the gauge field.**  Only the diagonal
`(μ, a) = (μ₀, a₀)` survives, and there the canonical relation `bookCCR` leaves the field and
ghost factors untouched. -/
theorem quartic_comm_Afield (μ0 : Fin 4) (a0 : Fin N) :
    (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
        (G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c)) * Afield μ0 a0
      - Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
        (G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c))
      = -((Complex.I : ℂ) • (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
          (G.f a0 b c) • (Afield μ0 b * chiOp c))) := by
  classical
  -- Distribute the commutator through the four sums.
  have hsplit :
      (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
          (G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c)) * Afield μ0 a0
        - Afield μ0 a0 * (∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
          (G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c))
      = ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ a : Fin N, ∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
          ((G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c) * Afield μ0 a0
            - Afield μ0 a0 * ((G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c))) := by
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => ?_
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun a _ => ?_
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => ?_
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  rw [hsplit]
  -- The term-wise commutator: only `π^μ_a` fails to commute, and it leaves `A_{μb} ψ†_c`.
  have hterm : ∀ (μ : Fin 4) (a b c : Fin N),
      (G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c) * Afield μ0 a0
          - Afield μ0 a0 * ((G.f a b c) • (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c))
        = (G.f a b c) • (-((if (μ0, a0) = (μ, a)
              then (Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) else 0)
                * (Afield μ b * chiOp c))) := by
    intro μ a b c
    have hcc : mom μ a * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom μ a
        = -((if (μ0, a0) = (μ, a)
            then (Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) else 0)) := by
      have hrearr : mom μ a * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom μ a
          = -((Afield μ0 a0 * mom μ a) - (mom μ a * Afield μ0 a0)) := by abel
      rw [hrearr, bookCCR μ0 μ a0 a]
    have hYW : (Afield (N := N) μ b * chiOp c) * Afield μ0 a0
        = Afield μ0 a0 * (Afield μ b * chiOp c) := by
      rw [mul_assoc, ← Afield_comm_chi μ0 a0 c, ← mul_assoc, Afield_comm_Afield μ μ0 b a0,
        mul_assoc]
    have hone : mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c * Afield μ0 a0
          - Afield μ0 a0 * (mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c)
        = (mom μ a * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * mom μ a) * (Afield μ b * chiOp c) := by
      rw [show mom μ a * Afield μ b * chiOp c = mom μ a * (Afield μ b * chiOp c) from
        mul_assoc (mom μ a) (Afield μ b) (chiOp c)]
      exact commutator_mul_right (U := mom μ a) (V := Afield μ b * chiOp c)
        (W := Afield μ0 a0) hYW
    rw [smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, ← smul_sub, hone, hcc, neg_mul]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun a _ =>
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun c _ => hterm μ a b c]
  -- Collapse the `(μ, a)` sums: only the diagonal survives.
  have hoff : ∀ (μ : Fin 4) (a : Fin N), (μ, a) ≠ (μ0, a0) →
      (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
        (G.f a b c) • (-((if (μ0, a0) = (μ, a)
              then (Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) else 0)
                * (Afield μ b * chiOp c)))) = 0 := by
    intro μ a h
    have hif : (if (μ0, a0) = (μ, a)
        then (Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) else 0)
        = (0 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) := if_neg (Ne.symm h)
    rw [hif]
    simp
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single μ0
    (fun μ _ hμ => Finset.sum_eq_zero fun a _ =>
      hoff μ a (by intro h; exact hμ (congrArg Prod.fst h)))
    (fun hh => absurd (Finset.mem_univ μ0) hh)]
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single a0
    (fun a _ ha => hoff μ0 a (by intro h; exact ha (congrArg Prod.snd h)))
    (fun hh => absurd (Finset.mem_univ a0) hh)]
  -- Evaluate the diagonal and pull the `i` out of the remaining two sums.
  have hdiag : ∀ b c : Fin N,
      (G.f a0 b c) • (-((if (μ0, a0) = (μ0, a0)
            then (Complex.I • 1 : Module.End ℂ (BookState N)) else 0)
              * (Afield μ0 b * chiOp c)))
        = -((Complex.I : ℂ) • ((G.f a0 b c) • (Afield μ0 b * chiOp c))) := by
    intro b c
    rw [if_pos rfl, smul_one_mul_end, smul_neg, smul_comm]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun c _ => hdiag b c]
  simp only [Finset.sum_neg_distrib, ← Finset.smul_sum]

/-- **The non-abelian BRST variation of the gauge field.**

`[Ω, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −i · dChi G μ₀ a₀ + i · Σ_{b,c} f_{a₀bc} A_{μ₀b} ψ†_c`,

i.e. `[Ω, A_{μ₀a₀}] = −i (D_{μ₀}ψ†)_{a₀}`: the ghost-dressed **longitudinal** direction plus
the **non-abelian commutator** part `[A_μ, α]`.  The first summand is the derivative term (the
whole answer in the abelian case); the second is the term `softmodes.md` Phase 1 item 3 recorded
as "a shape, not a theorem", and it is field-dependent, so it is not a gradient.  This is why in
the non-abelian theory the gauge orbit is strictly larger than the longitudinal span, and why the
identification must be read as `longitudinal ⊆ gauge orbit = exact`. -/
theorem comm_bookOmega_Afield_nonabelian (μ0 : Fin 4) (a0 : Fin N) :
    bookOmega G * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * bookOmega G
      = -((Complex.I : ℂ) • dChi G μ0 a0)
        + (Complex.I : ℂ) • (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N,
            (G.f a0 b c) • (Afield μ0 b * chiOp c)) := by
  classical
  have hkey : ∀ A Q R : Module.End ℂ (BookState N),
      (A - Q - R) * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * (A - Q - R)
        = (A * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * A)
          - (Q * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * Q)
          - (R * Afield μ0 a0 - Afield μ0 a0 * R) := by
    intro A Q R
    rw [sub_mul, sub_mul, mul_sub, mul_sub]
    abel
  have hR : ((Complex.I / 2) • (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N, ∑ e : Fin N,
        (G.f b c e) • (chiOp b * chiOp c * betaOp e))) * Afield μ0 a0
      - Afield μ0 a0 * ((Complex.I / 2) • (∑ b : Fin N, ∑ c : Fin N, ∑ e : Fin N,
        (G.f b c e) • (chiOp b * chiOp c * betaOp e))) = 0 := by
    rw [smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, ghostCubic_comm_Afield G μ0 a0, sub_self]
  rw [bookOmega, hkey, comm_deriv_Afield G μ0 a0, quartic_comm_Afield G μ0 a0, hR, sub_zero]
  abel

end

end BookProof.BrstLongitudinal
